[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3814423749","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115498#issuecomment-3814423749","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115498","id":3814423749,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7jW3zF","user":{"login":"geekley","id":38332912,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4MzMyOTEy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38332912?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley","html_url":"https://github.com/geekley","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-28T23:17:18Z","updated_at":"2026-01-28T23:17:18Z","body":"Would it not be possible to do the `if method.getName() == \"println\":` part automatically from godot for every java interface method, and use godot reflection to `callv` the appropriate method? So we pass a godot object (potentially with multiple methods) instead of a single callback, just like how we would create an anonymous object in Java?","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3814423749/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3814507757","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115498#issuecomment-3814507757","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115498","id":3814507757,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7jXMTt","user":{"login":"m4gr3d","id":914968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNDk2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/914968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d","html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-28T23:39:32Z","updated_at":"2026-01-28T23:39:32Z","body":"> Would it not be possible to do the `if method.getName() == \"println\":` part automatically from godot for every java interface method, and use godot reflection to `callv` the appropriate method? So we pass a godot object (potentially with multiple methods) instead of a single callback, just like how we would create an anonymous object in Java?\r\n\r\nyes, that's doable. I'd make it a separate method so the callable approach can be used for SAM interfaces, and an object with multiple methods can be used for interfaces with multiple methods.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3814507757/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3814603172","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115498#issuecomment-3814603172","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115498","id":3814603172,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7jXjmk","user":{"login":"geekley","id":38332912,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4MzMyOTEy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38332912?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley","html_url":"https://github.com/geekley","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/geekley/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-29T00:13:05Z","updated_at":"2026-01-29T00:13:05Z","body":"> so the callable approach can be used for SAM interfaces\r\n\r\nJust to check if I understand correctly.\r\nIf it's a single-method interface, could I drop the `if method.getName() == \"println\":` because that would be always true? (as it seems toString, hashCode and equals are handled already)\r\nAnd is `method: JavaObject` a `java.lang.reflect.Method`? It's worth mentioning the `godotCallable: Callable`'s parameter types in the javadoc.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3814603172/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3820842300","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115498#issuecomment-3820842300","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115498","id":3820842300,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7jvW08","user":{"login":"m4gr3d","id":914968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNDk2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/914968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d","html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-29T22:58:19Z","updated_at":"2026-01-29T22:58:19Z","body":"> > so the callable approach can be used for SAM interfaces\r\n> \r\n> Just to check if I understand correctly. If it's a single-method interface, could I drop the `if method.getName() == \"println\":` because that would be always true? (as it seems toString, hashCode and equals are handled already) And is `method: JavaObject` a `java.lang.reflect.Method`? It's worth mentioning the `godotCallable: Callable`'s parameter types in the javadoc.\r\n\r\n@geekley I've changed things a bit. We now have two methods:\r\n- `create_sam_callback(sam_interface, callable)`: As its name indicates, this creates a callback that implements the given SAM interface. The internal logic validates the given interface is indeed a SAM interface, and fails otherwise. Given it's a SAM interface, the passed callable can just focus on implementing that SAM interface method, as in it should expect arguments types matching the single abstract method's arguments types, and its return type must match the single asbtract method's return type.\r\n- `create_proxy(object, interfaces)`: This creates a proxy object that implements the given interfaces, and use the given object for its implementation. The object's methods signatures must match the signatures of the given interfaces' methods as calls to the interfaces methods are dispatched to the object using Godot reflection.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3820842300/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4171987364","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115498#issuecomment-4171987364","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115498","id":4171987364,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc74q3mk","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-01T18:03:39Z","updated_at":"2026-04-01T18:03:39Z","body":"Thanks!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4171987364/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":4,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]